IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa24-delivery`

-- coa24-tests-delivery.l4: tests for ss 1111 and 1113 to 1119 (coa24-delivery.l4). Expected values decided from the text
-- before the run; dates are worked out by hand.

§ `Tests for s 1111`

#ASSERT `s 1111(1) the registrar may impose requirements as to the person by whom the certificate or verification is to be given` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1111(1) the registrar may impose requirements as to the person by whom the certificate or verification is to be given` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1111(1) the registrar may impose requirements as to the person by whom the certificate or verification is to be given` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1111(1) the registrar may impose requirements as to the person by whom the certificate or verification is to be given` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1111(2) the power conferred by section 1068 is exercisable in relation to the certificate or verification as if it were a separate document` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1111(2) the power conferred by section 1068 is exercisable in relation to the certificate or verification as if it were a separate document` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1111(3) the registrar may impose the requirement` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1111(3) the registrar may impose the requirement` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests for s 1113`

#ASSERT `s 1113(1) the section applies` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1113(1) the section applies` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1113(1) the section applies` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (2): the registrar, or any member or creditor, may give notice.
#ASSERT `s 1113(2) the person may give notice to the company requiring it to comply with the obligation` (JUST TRUE) `s 1113 the registrar` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1113(2) the person may give notice to the company requiring it to comply with the obligation` (JUST TRUE) `s 1113 a member of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1113(2) the person may give notice to the company requiring it to comply with the obligation` (JUST TRUE) `s 1113 a creditor of the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1113(2) the person may give notice to the company requiring it to comply with the obligation` (JUST TRUE) `s 1113 some other person` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1113(2) the person may give notice to the company requiring it to comply with the obligation` NOTHING `s 1113 a member of the company` EQUALS NOTHING

-- (3): "within 14 days after service": notice served 1 March 2026, last day 15 March 2026.
#ASSERT `s 1113(3) the last day for the company to make good the default` (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS Date 15 3 2026
#ASSERT `s 1113(3) the last day for the company to make good the default` (Date 20 3 2026) EQUALS Date 3 4 2026
-- Made good on the last day (15 March): within the 14 days, so the "if" gate (failure to make good) is not met: not covered.
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 1113(3) the person may apply to the court for an order` (JUST TRUE) `s 1113 a member of the company` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 15 3 2026)) (Date 30 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE; name-test sweep (fork F20): the function is named for a grant or a power ("may apply to the court ... If the company fails to make good the default"), its gate is "if", and a failed "if" gate answers NOTHING, not the text's own no; the other reading, JUST FALSE, is in the fork register
#ASSERT `s 1113(3) the person may apply to the court for an order` (JUST TRUE) `s 1113 a member of the company` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 15 3 2026)) (Date 30 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Made good the day after (16 March): the company failed to make good within the 14 days.
#ASSERT `s 1113(3) the person may apply to the court for an order` (JUST TRUE) `s 1113 a member of the company` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 16 3 2026)) (Date 30 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not made good, asked on the last day: the 14 days have not ended, so the "if" gate is not met: not covered.
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 1113(3) the person may apply to the court for an order` (JUST TRUE) `s 1113 the registrar` (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING (Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE; name-test sweep (fork F20): the function is named for a grant or a power ("may apply to the court ... If the company fails to make good the default"), its gate is "if", and a failed "if" gate answers NOTHING, not the text's own no; the other reading, JUST FALSE, is in the fork register
#ASSERT `s 1113(3) the person may apply to the court for an order` (JUST TRUE) `s 1113 the registrar` (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING (Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not made good, asked the day after: the registrar may apply.
#ASSERT `s 1113(3) the person may apply to the court for an order` (JUST TRUE) `s 1113 the registrar` (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING (Date 16 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1113(3) the person may apply to the court for an order` (JUST TRUE) `s 1113 a creditor of the company` (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING (Date 16 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Anyone else is not named in the subsection.
#ASSERT `s 1113(3) the person may apply to the court for an order` (JUST TRUE) `s 1113 some other person` (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING (Date 16 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The section does not apply, or its application is not known.
#ASSERT `s 1113(3) the person may apply to the court for an order` NOTHING `s 1113 the registrar` (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING (Date 16 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

-- The regulative rule: day 0 is the day of service. Made good on day 14: FULFILLED. On day 15: BREACH. Never: BREACH.
#TRACE `s 1113(3) the company's duty to make good the default` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 1113(3) the company` DOES `s 1113(3) make good the default` AT 14

#TRACE `s 1113(3) the company's duty to make good the default` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 1113(3) the company` DOES `s 1113(3) make good the default` AT 15

#TRACE `s 1113(3) the company's duty to make good the default` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 15)

#ASSERT `s 1113(4) the court's order may provide that costs are borne by the company or by officers of it responsible for the default` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1113(4) the court's order may provide that costs are borne by the company or by officers of it responsible for the default` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1113(5) section 1113 affects the operation of the enactment` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1113(5) section 1113 affects the operation of the enactment` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests for s 1114`

#ASSERT `s 1114(1)(a) the thing is a document in Part 35` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1114(1)(a) the thing is a document in Part 35` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1114(1)(b) the act is delivering a document` `s 1114(1)(b) forwarding` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1114(1)(b) the act is delivering a document` `s 1114(1)(b) lodging` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1114(1)(b) the act is delivering a document` `s 1114(1)(b) registering` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1114(1)(b) the act is delivering a document` `s 1114(1)(b) sending` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1114(1)(b) the act is delivering a document` `s 1114(1)(b) producing` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1114(1)(b) the act is delivering a document` `s 1114(1)(b) submitting` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1114(1)(b) the act is delivering a document` `s 1114(1)(b) giving a notice` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1114(1)(b) the act is delivering a document` `s 1114(1)(b) providing information by virtue of section 1110E or any other enactment authorising the disclosure of information to the registrar` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1114(1)(b) the act is delivering a document` `s 1114(1)(b) some other act` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1114(2) Part 35 applies to the supply of the information as it applies to the delivery of a document` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1114(2) Part 35 applies to the supply of the information as it applies to the delivery of a document` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1114(2) Part 35 applies to the supply of the information as it applies to the delivery of a document` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests for ss 1115 to 1119`

#ASSERT `s 1115(2) the document must be authenticated in the manner specified by registrar's rules` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1115(2) the document must be authenticated in the manner specified by registrar's rules` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1115(2) the document must be authenticated in the manner specified by registrar's rules` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 1116(1) the notice may instead be published by the approved means` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1116(1) the notice may instead be published by the approved means` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1116(1) the notice may instead be published by the approved means` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1116(5) the registrar meets the requirement of s 1116(5)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1116(5) the registrar meets the requirement of s 1116(5)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1116(5) the registrar meets the requirement of s 1116(5)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1116(6) this section prevents the registrar from giving public notice both in the Gazette and by approved means` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1116(6) this section prevents the registrar from giving public notice both in the Gazette and by approved means` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The requirement of public notice is met when notice is first given by either means: the earlier day.
#ASSERT `s 1116(6) the day on which the requirement of public notice is met` (JUST (Date 10 3 2026)) (JUST (Date 12 3 2026)) EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2026)
#ASSERT `s 1116(6) the day on which the requirement of public notice is met` (JUST (Date 12 3 2026)) (JUST (Date 10 3 2026)) EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2026)
#ASSERT `s 1116(6) the day on which the requirement of public notice is met` (JUST (Date 10 3 2026)) (JUST (Date 10 3 2026)) EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2026)
#ASSERT `s 1116(6) the day on which the requirement of public notice is met` (JUST (Date 10 3 2026)) NOTHING EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2026)
#ASSERT `s 1116(6) the day on which the requirement of public notice is met` NOTHING (JUST (Date 12 3 2026)) EQUALS JUST (Date 12 3 2026)
#ASSERT `s 1116(6) the day on which the requirement of public notice is met` NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 1117(3)(a) the registrar meets the requirement to publicise the rules` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1117(3)(a) the registrar meets the requirement to publicise the rules` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1117(3)(b) the registrar must make copies of the rules available to the public in the form` `hard copy form` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1117(3)(b) the registrar must make copies of the rules available to the public in the form` `electronic form` EQUALS JUST TRUE

#ASSERT `s 1118 the provision affects the operation in relation to the registrar of section 3(1) of the Government Trading Funds Act 1973` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1118 the provision affects the operation in relation to the registrar of section 3(1) of the Government Trading Funds Act 1973` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 1119(1) the registrar may direct that documents of the class be delivered to a specified address of the authorised person` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1119(1) the registrar may direct that documents of the class be delivered to a specified address of the authorised person` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1119(1) the direction meets the requirement of s 1119(1)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1119(1) the direction meets the requirement of s 1119(1)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1119(1) the direction meets the requirement of s 1119(1)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1119(2) the document is treated as delivered` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1119(2) the document is treated as delivered` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1119(2) the document is treated as delivered` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1119(3) the provision is subordinate legislation for the purposes of section 71 of the Deregulation and Contracting Out Act 1994` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1119(3) the provision is subordinate legislation for the purposes of section 71 of the Deregulation and Contracting Out Act 1994` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
